{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-descent-cocycle-deviation","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:descent-cocycle-deviation","kind":"lemma","title":"Cocycle deviation recursion at level $n+1$ (hypothesis)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-yekutieli-triple"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-descent-cocycle-deviation"],"tags":["cocycle","yekutieli-triple","central-extension","cech-cohomology"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.descent_cocycle_deviation","text":"descent-cocycle-deviation.md","leanSource":"descent-cocycle-deviation.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:descent-cocycle-deviation\"></a><p><em>Under the central extension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_{n+1} \\to \\mathfrak{G}_n</code> with local lift data <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a_{ij}^{(n)} \\in \\mathcal{O}_M^{\\times}</code>, assume the cocycle deviation at level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n+1</code> is given by the recursion</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  g_{ijk}^{(n+1)}\n  =\n  a_{ij}^{(n)} \\cdot a_{jk}^{(n)} \\cdot (a_{ik}^{(n)})^{-1}\n  \\cdot g_{ijk}^{(n)}.</code></pre>\n<p><em>Then the recursion holds at every level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> and for every triple <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(i, j, k)</code>.</em></p>\n<p><em>This lemma records the recursion as a hypothesis of the descent context; it does not derive it. Whether <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g^{(n)}</code> satisfies a twisted Čech <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-cocycle equation, and whether it defines a class in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^2(M, \\mathcal{O}_M^{\\times})</code>, is not part of this statement.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-cocycle-deviation.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"6.10.7","page":"b/lem-descent-cocycle-deviation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":94,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.descent_cocycle_deviation","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-cocycle-deviation.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
